      <floats-group id="article-26710.s12">
        <fig id="article-26710.image.f5" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Graphical Representation of Henry's Law. This plot demonstrates the relationship between partial pressure and liquid species composition, highlighting the linear range where Henry's law remains applicable. The data points illustrate how real solutions begin to diverge from the ideal behavior predicted by the law as concentration increases. Specifically, Henry&#x02019;s law is valid at low solute concentrations but is not applicable at higher concentrations. Contributed by KM Tenny, PhD, MS</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="henry_ppt" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
        </fig>
      </floats-group>
